.TH FSCK.SIEFS 8
.SH NAME
fsck.siefs \- check a SieFS image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B build/host/fsck.siefs
.RB [ \-d ]
.I image
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fsck.siefs
runs on the build machine (Linux). It checks every checksum, the trees,
the free space, the link counts and the attribute index, and prints each
problem, then how many. The tests run it on their disks after SIEOS
powers off.
.PP
Repairing is not needed after a crash: a commit is all or nothing, and a
damaged image falls back to the previous commit when mounted.
.PP
An image a running QEMU is using is not checked ("in use by another
program"): what it holds then is changing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Also read and check every data block.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 clean; 1 problems found; 2 the image cannot be mounted, or is in use.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR siefs (8),
.BR mkfs.siefs (8),
.BR siefs (5)
